# Wi-Fi names and passwords compiled into the firmware (sdkconfig syntax).
#
# 1. Create config/secrets.local (git-ignored) in one of two ways:
#      python tools/repeater.py init-secrets      (random passwords)
#    or copy this file to config/secrets.local and replace every REPLACE_ME.
# 2. Check it:  python tools/repeater.py check-secrets
#
# Step-by-step explanation: docs/FLASHING_GUIDE.md, step 4.
#
# What the values do
#   Repeater network    The Wi-Fi the board broadcasts; phones and laptops join
#   (SETUP_AP_*)        it. Also the way to reach the setup page at
#                       http://192.168.4.1 (or CONFIG_REPEATER_AP_IP).
#   Admin password      Login for that web page (and the remote console, if you
#                       enable it). Keep it different from the Wi-Fi passwords:
#                       people you give Wi-Fi access should not be able to
#                       reconfigure the repeater.
#   Uplink (optional)   The existing 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi the board connects to and
#                       repeats. Leave both lines commented out to choose it on
#                       the Getting Started page instead.
#   AP address          The repeater's own address; clients get the same /24.
#   (optional)          Only change it for a second board that connects to the
#                       first one (use 192.168.5.1 there).
#
# Rules (enforced at build time)
#   - SSIDs: up to 31 bytes, no control characters; the repeater network name
#     must not be empty and must differ from the uplink name.
#   - Passwords: 8-63 printable ASCII characters. The uplink password may be
#     empty for an open network.
#   - No double quote (") or backslash (\), no leading or trailing space, and
#     no '??' followed by = ( / ) ' < ! > - (a C trigraph).
#   - Admin password: at most 127 bytes once URL-encoded (each symbol counts
#     as 3), because the web login field is 128 bytes.
#   - AP address: dotted quad with a last number of 1-254, e.g. 192.168.4.1.
#
# These values are used when the board has no saved settings: on first boot,
# after `flash --erase`, and after a factory reset (BOOT held 5 s). Settings
# saved later on the device (web page or serial commands) take precedence.
# The firmware image embeds these values: never share build/ output.

# Repeater network (required)
CONFIG_REPEATER_SETUP_AP_SSID="ESP32-Repeater-Setup"
CONFIG_REPEATER_SETUP_AP_PASSWORD="REPLACE_ME_8_to_63_chars"

# Web page login (required)
CONFIG_REPEATER_ADMIN_PASSWORD="REPLACE_ME_different_8_to_63_chars"

# Existing Wi-Fi to repeat (optional: remove the leading "# " to use)
# CONFIG_REPEATER_UPLINK_SSID="REPLACE_ME_existing_wifi_name"
# CONFIG_REPEATER_UPLINK_PASSWORD="REPLACE_ME_existing_wifi_password"

# Repeater address (optional)
# CONFIG_REPEATER_AP_IP="192.168.4.1"
